# config/privacy-rail.list.example -- operator-designated rail privacy list (2026-10-23).
# Install as /etc/corporatetraveldc/privacy-rail.list (root-owned, 0640; the operator
# account must be able to read it for push-time checks). One entry per line; # comments.
# Read by scripts/leak-guard/privacy_lists.py: matched only in rail context, reported as
# 'rail-identifier', values never printed. Missing or empty file = "no entries"
# (reported, never a failure). Real entries never go in this tracked example.
#
# id:<identifier>    matched only after a rail key (train, train_id, trainset, consist,
#                    locomotive, loco, railcar)
# Synthetic examples, left commented:
# id:QQSYN0001
# id:QR-0000
